The Composite API with `allOrNone: true` is the right tool here. Since `Service_Request__c` has no lookup field to Asset, there's no reference-field linkage needed between subrequest 2 and 3 — the trigger looks up the Asset by `SerialNumber` after it's been committed in the transaction (the Composite API wraps all subrequests in one transaction, so the Asset insert happens before the Service_Request insert, and the trigger's SOQL will see it since it's the same transaction/database state at that point).

The Account must be created first, then the Asset (using `@{newAccount.id}` for the AccountId lookup), then the Service_Request record last, with `allOrNone` set to true so any failure rolls back everything.

